# 14. Trade-Off Analysis

## Advantages

✅ Effective in high-dimensional spaces  
✅ Powerful maximum-margin principle  
✅ Can model nonlinear boundaries using kernels  
✅ Works well with appropriately sized datasets  
✅ Often effective when the feature space is larger than the number of samples  

---

## Disadvantages

❌ Can be computationally expensive on large datasets  
❌ Sensitive to scaling  
❌ Kernel and hyperparameter selection can be difficult  
❌ Less interpretable than simple linear models  
❌ Probability estimates can require additional calibration/computation

---

# 15. SVM vs Logistic Regression

| Feature | Logistic Regression | SVM |
|---|---|---|
| Main Goal | Model class probabilities | Find maximum-margin boundary |
| Output | Natural probability model | Decision scores by default |
| Nonlinear Extension | Feature engineering / other methods | Kernels |
| Scaling | Often beneficial | Very important |
| Interpretability | Higher | Can be lower |

### Interview Answer

> Logistic Regression optimizes a probabilistic classification objective, while SVM focuses on finding a decision boundary with maximum margin. SVM can also use kernels to model nonlinear boundaries.

